{"type":"message","id":"328461ea","parentId":"e2666b8a","timestamp":"2026-05-16T03:38:52.144Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All POST attempts are failing with 401. Let me check if the issue is with the endpoint path. The API used `/history` with X-API-Key header. Maybe I need to look at what the actual POST endpoint format is. The GET to /send just returned \"Unauthorized\" which means it's not the auth issue but the method.\n\nWait - actually looking at the very first attempts, both GET /history requests returned \"Unauthorized\" with the Bearer token but worked with X-API-Key. The curl verbose showed the request went through properly.\n\nFor POST, X-API-Key also failed. Maybe the POST endpoint genuinely requires a different auth that isn't available. \n\nBut this is a cron job that's been running, so the previous agent must have found a way to authenticate. Let me look back at the heartbeat messages to see how they were originally posted. The messages show IDs like msg_1778900910187_8gxwal, which suggests they came from somewhere. Maybe POST requests need a completely different auth scheme? Let me try sending a Basic auth header with the API key as the password, or double-check whether the Content-Type header might be the issue instead.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-f5d1f388-2c52-4c0f-8b6c-7bb77849a883","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with Basic auth\ncurl -s -w \"\\nHTTP_CODE: %{http_code}\\n\" -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Basic echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-c0dc84ec-4b1d-4272-995f-7cf844eece50","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check if there's an API documentation or endpoint info\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyat